  "body": "This PR is the `xtask` part of #2908. It does not change `post-merge.yml`. The issue stays open for the workflow.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --lane N/M` runs lane N of M of the batch plan (new module `xtask/src/lane_split.rs`).\n  - The split is a round-robin deal in plan order. It reads no timing file. Thus each runner computes the same lanes for the same commit.\n  - Each test step and clippy is in exactly one lane. The steps that share the machine are dealt first, then the steps that run alone (`lanes::ISOLATED`, ui, clippy).\n  - A lane keeps the `debug build: <crate>` step of each crate that it tests.\n  - `--lane 1/1` is the full batch plan of today.\n  - The batch plan of this repository has 973 steps. Three lanes get 325, 324 and 324 steps.\n- A lane run writes `lane-result.tsv` into its `gate-logs/batch-<stamp>/` (new module `xtask/src/verdict.rs`). The record has the lane, the runner name (`RUNNER_NAME`), the result, the wall time, the planned step count and one row for each step that ran.\n- `cargo xtask gate-verdict <dir>...` reads the records below the directories and prints one Markdown verdict. The verdict names each lane, its runner, its time, its result and its record path, then each red step with its note. The exit code is 0 for green and 1 for red.\n- Refusals, each with a message:\n  - `--lane` on a tier that is not `batch`.\n  - A lane that is not `N/M` with `1 <= N <= M <= 16`.\n  - A lane with no step.\n- The verdict is red when a lane has no record, has two records, is void, ran fewer steps than its plan, or has a record that cannot be read.\n- `xtask/src/exec.rs`: the field `clock` of `Run` is `pub(crate)`, so that the record can read the wall time.\n- `.claude/skills/gate/SKILL.md`: a section \"Batch lanes for separate runners\" and the flag row.\n- `docs/decisions/2908-batch-lanes.md`: the decisions.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe batch tier had no deterministic way to run as parts. `post-merge.yml` thus runs all 973 steps in one job on one runner, and the second runner waits. A lane job also had no result file that a collector could read.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins, in `xtask/src/lane_split_tests.rs` and `xtask/src/verdict_tests.rs` (14 tests):\n\n- `each_batch_step_runs_in_exactly_one_lane` (the real batch plan, 1 to 6 lanes: no step lost, no step in two lanes)\n- `one_lane_of_one_is_the_whole_batch_plan`\n- `a_lane_builds_each_crate_that_it_tests_before_the_tests`\n- `the_lanes_share_the_queued_and_the_alone_steps_evenly`\n- `the_split_is_the_same_on_each_call_and_reads_no_timing_file`\n- `a_bad_lane_is_refused_by_name`\n- `a_lane_with_no_step_is_an_error_not_a_green_run`\n- `a_record_reads_back_as_written`\n- `a_damaged_record_is_an_error`\n- `all_lanes_green_is_a_green_verdict_that_names_each_lane`\n- `a_red_step_is_named_with_its_lane_runner_and_note`\n- `a_missing_a_double_a_void_or_a_short_lane_is_red`\n- `the_runner_name_comes_from_the_environment`\n- `the_collector_finds_the_records_of_downloaded_artifacts`\n\nRed before the change: `cargo xtask gate batch --lane 1/2 --dry-run` on `upstream/main` `0306743de` gives `xtask: unknown gate option '--lane'`.\n\nMutation results (each mutation made the named pin red; the restored code is green):\n\n| Mutation | Red pins |\n|---|---|\n| The alone steps get no lane | `each_batch_step_runs_in_exactly_one_lane` and 3 others |\n| No build step is kept | `a_lane_builds_each_crate_that_it_tests_before_the_tests`, `one_lane_of_one_is_the_whole_batch_plan` |\n| `N > M` is accepted | `a_bad_lane_is_refused_by_name`, `a_damaged_record_is_an_error` |\n| An empty lane is not an error | `a_lane_with_no_step_is_an_error_not_a_green_run` |\n| `--lane` is accepted on each tier | `a_bad_lane_is_refused_by_name` |\n| A missing lane is not a fault | `a_missing_a_double_a_void_or_a_short_lane_is_red`, `the_collector_finds_the_records_of_downloaded_artifacts` |\n| A short lane is not a fault | `a_missing_a_double_a_void_or_a_short_lane_is_red` |\n| A void lane is not a fault | `a_missing_a_double_a_void_or_a_short_lane_is_red` |\n| The red steps are not listed | `a_red_step_is_named_with_its_lane_runner_and_note` |\n\nWith the `main.rs` of `upstream/main` restored, the new test modules are not part of the build, and no pin runs. That restore is not a red test. The CLI error above is the red reading.\n\nReadings on Linux:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (`xtask unit tests`, 251 s).\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --lane 1/3 --dry-run`: 9 builds, then 325 of 973 steps. Lane 3: 324 steps.\n- One real lane step: `cargo xtask gate batch --lane 1/3 --only \"cl suites: lib\"` was green and wrote `lane-result.tsv`.\n- `cargo xtask gate-verdict gate-logs` on that one record: verdict RED, exit code 1, \"lane 2/3 has no record\" and \"lane 3/3 has no record\". This is correct for one lane of three.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No full lane ran. Only one step of lane 1/3 ran for real.\n- No GitHub Actions run. No workflow uses the lanes. The record was not written on a self-hosted runner, so `RUNNER_NAME` was not set (the record said `unknown`).\n- Windows and macOS.\n- The time balance of the lanes. The lanes have equal step counts, not equal measured times.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2606 (`needs-maintainer`) changes the `report` job of `.github/workflows/post-merge.yml`. This PR does not change that file. The workflow part of #2908 waits for the decision on #2606.\n- #2787 (`needs-rework`, `conflicts`) changes `parse_gate` and `gate` in `xtask/src/main.rs` (a new tier). It touches the same functions, different lines. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #2910 and #2915 list many `xtask/` files because their branches carry a process file sync. They do not change the lane code.\n\nProcess change: yes\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #2908\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
